<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">We estimate the c=
ost to collect, review, and produce the records to be $572.50.</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt; line-height:105%"><b=
><span style=3D"font-size:13.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:&quot;Calib=
ri&quot;,sans-serif">Fee Waiver Request Legal Standards</span></b></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt; line-height:105%"><s=
pan style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:&quot;Calibri&=
quot;,sans-serif">In reviewing a public records request fee waiver, we foll=
ow DAS Policy 107-001-030, the
<i>Attorney General=92s Public Records and Meetings Manual</i>, and Oregon=
=92s public records law. DAS Policy 107-001-030 provides the following guid=
ance:</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-right:.5in; margin-bottom:0in; mar=
gin-left:.75in; margin-bottom:.0001pt; text-indent:-.25in; line-height:105%=
">
<span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:Symbol"><spa=
n style=3D"mso-list:Ignore">=B7<span style=3D"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Ro=
man&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; fon=
t-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">To adequately balance the State's =
obligation to be transparent and accessible with the obligation to prudentl=
y safeguard public funds and resources, fee-waivers
 and -reductions should be granted when the statutory standard has been met=
 =96 when disclosure will primarily benefit the general public.
</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-right:.5in; margin-bottom:0in; mar=
gin-left:.75in; margin-bottom:.0001pt; text-indent:-.25in; line-height:105%=
">
<span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:Symbol"><spa=
n style=3D"mso-list:Ignore">=B7<span style=3D"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Ro=
man&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; fon=
t-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">A request to waive or reduce fees =
related to a public records request, that requires substantial agency resou=
rces to complete, may be denied if the interest
 of the general public would be better served by preserving agency resource=
s. </span>
</p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-right:.5in; margin-bottom:0in; mar=
gin-left:.75in; margin-bottom:.0001pt; text-indent:-.25in; line-height:105%=
">
<span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:Symbol"><spa=
n style=3D"mso-list:Ignore">=B7<span style=3D"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Ro=
man&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; fon=
t-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">The public interest is not a fixed=
 concept and the balance of public interest may change over time. It may sh=
ift as information becomes older or in the light
 of issues of the day. The circumstances at the time of the request will be=
 considered.</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-right:.5in; margin-bottom:0in; mar=
gin-left:.75in; margin-bottom:.0001pt; text-indent:-.25in; line-height:105%=
">
<span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:Symbol"><spa=
n style=3D"mso-list:Ignore">=B7<span style=3D"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Ro=
man&quot;">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span></span></span><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; fon=
t-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">A genuine public interest in the s=
ubject matter of a request is required as the basis for granting a waiver. =
The public interest is not necessarily the same
 as what interests the public. The fact that a topic has been discussed in =
the media does not automatically mean that there is a public interest in di=
sclosing the information that has been requested about it.</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-right:.5in; margin-bottom:0in; mar=
gin-left:.75in; margin-bottom:.0001pt; line-height:105%">
<span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:&quot;Calibr=
i&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt; line-height:105%"><s=
pan style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:&quot;Calibri&=
quot;,sans-serif">ORS 192.324 (5) allows the custodian of a public record t=
o waive or reduce the fee associated with a public
 records request if disclosure of the record at issue =93=85 primarily bene=
fits the general public.=94 Waiving or reducing fees is in the public inter=
est =93when the furnishing of the record has utility - indeed, its greatest=
 utility - to the community or society as
 a whole.=94 <i>In Def. of Animals v. Or. Health Sciences Univ.</i>, 199 Or=
 App 160, 189 (2005). The custodian of the record may deny a request for a =
full or partial fee waiver even if disclosure would primarily benefit the p=
ublic, provided that the denial is
 reasonable under the totality of the circumstances.<i> Id.</i> at 189-90.<=
/span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt; line-height:105%"><s=
pan style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:&quot;Calibri&=
quot;,sans-serif">Waiving or reducing fees in the public interest is distin=
ct from situations where disclosure would primarily
 affect a concern or interest of a private individual.<i> Id.</i> at 188. R=
elevant factors to consider when determining whether a requester has establ=
ished a sufficient public interest include: (1) the requester=92s identity,=
 (2) the purpose for which the requester
 intends to use the information, (3) the character of the information, (4) =
whether the requested information is already in the public domain, and (5) =
whether the requester can demonstrate the ability to disseminate the inform=
ation to the public.
<i>See</i> <i>State of Oregon, Department of Justice,</i> <i>Atty. Gen. Pub=
lic Records and Meetings Manual</i>, 19-20 (2024).</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt; line-height:105%"><b=
><span style=3D"font-size:13.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:&quot;Calib=
ri&quot;,sans-serif">Fee Waiver Request Analysis</span></b></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">Applying the relevant factors helps us determine=
 whether the PRR is in the public interest. The requester has demonstrated =
that this request relates to a personal, rather
 than a public interest. Therefore, this factor does not weigh in favor of =
granting a fee waiver.</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">The second factor is the purpose for which the r=
equester intends to use the information. The requester has not demonstrated=
 that this factor weighs in favor of granting
 a fee waiver as the use of records for a personal issue does not weigh in =
favor of the request being in the public interest.</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">The third factor is the character of the informa=
tion. The requester has not demonstrated that this factor weighs in favor o=
f granting a fee waiver as the fee waiver request
 form does not explain how the release of records is in the public interest=
 other than by stating a general interest in transparency.</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">The fourth factor is whether the requested infor=
mation is already in the public domain. The requester has not demonstrated =
that this factor weighs in favor of granting a
 fee waiver.</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">The final factor is whether the requester can de=
monstrate the ability to disseminate the information to the public. The req=
uester has not demonstrated the ability to disseminate
 the public records but merely stated that he can post it on a website.</sp=
an></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; font-family:&quot=
;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt; line-height:105%"><s=
pan style=3D"font-size:11.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:&quot;Calibri&=
quot;,sans-serif">Finally, in evaluating a public records request fee waive=
r the public body must consider whether, under the
 totality of the circumstances, a fee waiver is also in the public interest=
. When weighing the public interest in disclosure versus the public interes=
t in preserving public funds, when none of the prescribed factors weigh in =
favor of the grant of a fee waiver,
 the grant of a fee waiver is not warranted. Consequently, your request for=
 a fee waiver is denied.</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal" style=3D"margin-bottom:8.0pt; line-height:105%"><b=
><span style=3D"font-size:13.0pt; line-height:105%; font-family:&quot;Calib=
ri&quot;,sans-serif">Fee Payment</span></b><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt;=
 line-height:105%">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">I will wait to he=
ar from you prior to proceeding with the collection and review of these rec=
ords. If you decide to pay the $572.50, we will send you instructions on su=
bmitting payment.&nbsp;Let me know if you
 have any questions. If you would like to narrow your request (for example =
by using a shorter date range, by searching only particular employee record=
s, or by adding search terms), I would be happy to work with you.</span></p=
>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p class=3D"x_MsoNormal"><span style=3D"font-size:11.0pt">Thanks,</span></p=
